1. Scope and definitions

This license applies only to contributions whose copyright holders have
offered them under this version or authorized the maintainer to do so.
Each grant is limited to rights that the granting party owns or controls.

The maintainer is the sole copyright holder of all first-party code in this repository. Every first-party contribution in this repository, regardless of which license version applied when it was committed, is offered under version 1.2 as of 17 November 2026. Bundled third-party components, including Markdown-it, the LobeHub assets and the bundled fonts, are not covered by this statement and remain under their own licenses, as recorded in web/vendor and web/fonts.

For the avoidance of doubt, the requirements in sections 3 and 5 concerning earlier contributions do not apply to first-party code authored by the maintainer, which is offered under this version as stated above.

It does not replace licenses on third-party components or retroactively
change the terms of earlier third-party contributions.

"Maintainer" means the operator of the muhdarifx GitHub account responsible
for the Goal-Layers repository.

"Personal use" means use for an individual's own projects or independent
learning, not work performed for an organization, client, or paid service.
The ownership of the computer and the time of use do not determine purpose.

"Organization" means a company, partnership, public body, nonprofit,
educational institution, or other legal entity. "Organizational use" means
use for that entity's work, including employee or contractor work,
internships, internal hackathons, and institution-operated teaching.
Independent student learning that is not work for an institution or client
is personal use.

"Internal use" means use within one identified legal entity by its staff
or contractors solely for that entity's work. Affiliates, clients, and
customers are not included unless a written agreement names them.

"Seat" means one distinct developer authorized to use Codex with Goal
Layers for the licensed entity. Count each such developer once across
devices and accounts. Shared accounts do not reduce the count. Count only
developers authorized to use Codex with Goal Layers, not every Codex user
in the organization.

"Commercial use" includes organizational use beyond the evaluation grant,
paid access, sale, rental, redistribution as part of a paid product or
service, and providing Goal Layers as a service to third parties. Charging
no separate fee, bundling access into another charge, or rebranding does
not remove these restrictions.

2. Personal use and free redistribution

Subject to this license, each participating copyright holder grants a
worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free copyright license to use, copy, and
modify their covered contributions for personal use.

You may redistribute covered source or binaries without charging for them
if you include this license and existing copyright notices, identify your
modifications, and give recipients no greater rights than this license
provides. Recipients receive their permissions directly from participating
copyright holders. This free redistribution grant does not allow paid
bundles, paid access, or commercial services.

3. Thirty-day internal evaluation

An organization may use, copy, and modify covered contributions internally
for one consecutive 30-day evaluation, without payment or a separate
written agreement. The evaluation begins on that entity's first
organizational use of code covered by this version. The entity must record
its legal name and start date internally; registration with the maintainer
is not required.

The evaluation permits staff and contractors to test compatibility,
usability, and suitability with the entity's own workflows and data,
including a limited internal pilot. It does not permit ongoing operational
deployment, paid services to clients, external hosted access, resale, or
sublicensing. There is no seat cap during evaluation.

One legal entity receives one evaluation period; another installation,
user, version, or reinstall does not restart it. At its end, stop
organizational use and remove operational copies unless a written
commercial agreement is in force. Inactive backups and the entity's own
data may be retained, but do not grant continued use of the software.

This evaluation covers only code authorized under this version. Earlier
contributions not relicensed by their owners remain subject to their
existing terms. The maintainer must obtain those permissions or exclude
that code before offering it under this evaluation.

4. Commercial and ongoing organizational use

A separate written agreement from the relevant rights holders or their
authorized representative is required for commercial use beyond section
3. An internal-use agreement must identify the licensed legal entity,
authorized seat count, permitted use, price, billing period, and start/end
dates. No commercial price, royalty, revenue percentage, billing period,
automatic renewal, or obligation to buy is established by this license.

Unless the agreement expressly states otherwise, it permits only the
named entity's internal use. It grants no right to redistribute, sublicense,
resell, provide third-party hosted access, or include the software in a paid
product or service. Those activities need an express separate grant.

Unless the agreement expressly provides otherwise, either party may end
an ongoing internal-use agreement on 30 days' written notice to the other
party's designated contact. Agreed payment obligations and any refund
terms remain governed by that agreement. When permission ends, stop the
covered use and remove operational copies; inactive backups and the
customer's own data may be retained without continued software use.

Contact the repository maintainer through:
https://github.com/muhdarifx/Goal-Layers

A donation, tip, or code contribution does not purchase commercial rights.
The maintainer may grant rights only for code they own or are authorized
to license.

5. Contributions and permission to offer commercial licenses

Contributors retain ownership of their work. New contributions are accepted
