By that acknowledgment, the contributor confirms that they have authority
to grant these rights and identifies third-party material and its license.
They offer their contribution under this public license and also grant
the maintainer a worldwide, nonexclusive, perpetual, irrevocable,
royalty-free copyright license to use, reproduce, modify, prepare
derivative works, distribute, and sublicense that contribution under
commercial or other license terms. This does not transfer ownership or
require the contributor to give up other uses of their work.

The maintainer must obtain this acknowledgment before merging a new
contribution under these terms. Earlier contributions require their owners'
separate permission before being offered under version 1.2 or commercially
relicensed. This document does not assert that those permissions have
already been obtained. Third-party components retain their own terms.

6. Data and external services

This license transfers no ownership of the user's or organization's
session content, source code, prompts, outputs, or other data to the
maintainer. It grants no permission to collect that data.

Goal Layers can read local Codex records and save local snapshots, edits,
and review artifacts. Optional AI reviews and chat actions use Codex and
can transmit supplied content to the provider configured there. Users
remain responsible for the data they submit, access authorization, and
applicable provider terms. A network-restricted review fork does not
establish offline model processing.

Ending this license does not require deletion or surrender of the user's
own data, although it ends the applicable permission to use the software.

7. Breach and reserved rights

Permissions under this public license terminate if you violate its terms.
That termination takes effect 30 days after written notice describing the breach, if the breach remains uncured.
Stop the affected use and distribution when they terminate. This does not
alter permissions independently available under another valid license or
mandatory law. A separate commercial agreement may specify its own breach,
cure, and termination process.

No trademark rights are granted. Rights that cannot lawfully be restricted
remain unaffected. All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

